  "summary": "Low-fidelity edited images — amateur photos with alien text and eyes — evoking disorientation, nostalgia and unease.",
  "description": "Weirdcore edits ordinary snapshots with compression artifacts, displaced eyes, cryptic overlaid text (\"you are here forever\") and liminal emptiness, aiming for familiar-yet-wrong uncanniness rather than gore. It grew on imageboards and TikTok (2020s) alongside dreamcore and liminal spaces, drawing on analog horror and creepypasta imagery. It is best understood as a community-documented internet-native uncanny aesthetic.",
